WEBVTT

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:12.280
AV Room

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:11.400
And then

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:16.320
the woman led the policeman back to the bathroom.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:18.870
Following the policeman's instructions,

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:22.620
She went inside and waited to hear the voice again.

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:23.870
The creepy voice said,

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:26.830
"Do you want a red mantle?"

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:28.210
She then answered,

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:29.340
"Y-Yes."

00:00:29.340 --> 00:00:30.760
Then she answered...

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:37.550
The policeman hurried to open the door...

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:41.350
The woman inside was covered in blood, as though she was wearing a red mantle.

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:41.810
No way!

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:44.270
Mai! Don't use such a scary voice.

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:49.440
The story was over and another light turned off.

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:53.150
It's said that after finishing the last story, as you count off,

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:56.070
there'll be another person.

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:57.410
You're last, Michiru.

00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:00.330
The extra person is supposedly a ghost.

00:01:00.910 --> 00:01:03.450
Then, the story of the old school building, 'kay?

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:06.290
That story of the half-collapsed wooden building?

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:08.670
It's not "collapsed",

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:10.750
that's just where the demolition stopped.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:12.260
It's cursed!

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:16.550
In that old school building, students died.

00:01:16.550 --> 00:01:18.550
There was even a teacher who committed suicide.

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:21.310
While they were demolishing the west wall,

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:23.060
the roof collapsed.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:24.480
And then...

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:33.440
So the demolition was stopped.

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:37.450
The demolition was restarted last year in order to rebuild the gym.

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:43.160
But that time, a truck went out of control and drove through the field during class, killing some students.

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:44.700
What's more:

00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:47.460
I heard from an upperclassman,

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:51.290
that if you go by the old building at night...

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:00.800
Here we go...

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:01.850
One.

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:02.850
Two.

00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:03.850
Three.

00:02:04.310 --> 00:02:04.930
Four.

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:13.690
W-Was that you, just now?

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:15.650
Did I do something wrong?

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:17.320
What?!

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:18.990
I thought I was going to die.

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:19.990
Excuse me.

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:23.450
The light were out, so I thought nobody was in here until I heard voices...

00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:24.290
I just...

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.370
That is... it's alright.

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:31.920
What year are you in?

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:33.590
I'm seventeen this year.

00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:34.500
Huh?

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:37.720
Wouldn't someone normally just answer with "second year"?

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:37.720
That'd make you an upperclassman...

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:40.510
We were telling ghost stories.

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:41.590
Is that so?

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:43.140
Would you mind if I joined you?

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:46.180
You like ghost stories too?

00:02:46.180 --> 00:02:46.850
Well...

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:50.810
Um... Mind telling us your name?

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:51.440
Shibuya.

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:52.940
Shibuya Kazuya.

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:56.150
This person... his eyes aren't laughing.

00:02:56.480 --> 00:03:00.450
Um, Shibuya-san, what are you doing here?

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:02.110
I have some things to take care of.

00:03:02.110 --> 00:03:03.660
Then why don't you hurry up and...

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:04.950
We'll help!

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:06.370
Um...

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:07.200
No.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:10.290
How about, next time you tell ghost stories, let me join you.

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:12.210
Of course! In that case...

00:03:12.210 --> 00:03:13.840
how about tomorrow after class?

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:15.500
Alright. Where?

00:03:15.500 --> 00:03:17.090
Our homeroom...

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:18.970
Definitely suspicious.

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:20.720
This guy...

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:21.720
What is he planning?

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:56.560
Filled with Evil Spirits?!

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:01.530
What nice weather!

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:03.490
Leaving early today was a great idea!

00:05:03.950 --> 00:05:06.490
I have the cherry blossoms all to myself.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:18.580
now that I look at it,

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:20.750
those stories might be true.

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:23.760
What's that?

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:25.930
A video camera?

00:05:35.350 --> 00:05:36.480
As I thought, it is.

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:38.230
But what's it doing here?

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:39.940
Did they leave it behind?

00:05:39.940 --> 00:05:41.020
No way.

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:41.570
Who is it?!

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:44.440
I'm sorry...

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:45.530
It wasn't like I was--

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:48.360
N-No way!

00:06:06.340 --> 00:06:07.840
A-Are you alright?

00:06:09.140 --> 00:06:10.640
No! What should I do?

00:06:10.640 --> 00:06:11.680
Someone--

00:06:11.050 --> 00:06:11.680
What's wrong?

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:14.850
From yesterday...

00:06:17.690 --> 00:06:19.020
Lin, what happened?

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:23.520
It looks like a small cut. Can you stand?

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:24.070
Yes.

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:26.990
Um... I'm really sorry.

00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:28.910
I just heard a voice all of a sudden and then...

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:30.200
Never mind the excuses.

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:31.410
Is there a clinic close by?

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:34.580
There's one outside the school gate.

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:38.370
I'm fine.

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:40.370
I don't need your help.

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:44.920
We met yesterday, didn't we?

00:06:44.920 --> 00:06:45.800
What's your name?

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:47.720
Taniyama Mai.

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:48.840
Then, Taniyama-san.

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:51.590
I think I should let you know

00:06:51.590 --> 00:06:53.300
that the bell just rang.

00:06:55.310 --> 00:06:56.520
N-No way!

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:57.680
I'm late!!

00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:00.390
Really now! Just who are those guys?

00:07:00.390 --> 00:07:03.520
As I thought, that place is really bad luck..

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:08.650
Mai, you're going home?

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:11.110
What about the promise with Shibuya-senpai?

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:12.280
It's alright.

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:14.160
No way! I can't believe you!

00:07:14.160 --> 00:07:16.990
We were finally going to get to tell ghost stories together.

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:18.410
Ghost stories, is it?

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:21.290
That's what you're doing every day?

00:07:22.170 --> 00:07:24.630
No wonder I've been having headaches every day since I came here.

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:26.960
I'm sensitive to spirits.

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:29.170
So whenever spirits gather, I get headaches.

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:31.300
That's... our fault?

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:33.050
Of course it is!

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:36.220
Low level spirits gather when you tell ghost stories.

00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:38.220
Then they attract stronger spirits.

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:40.270
And if that happens, there'll be trouble.

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:43.020
So you shouldn't think of ghost stories as "fun".

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:44.310
You...

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:46.650
If you can sense spirits,

00:07:46.980 --> 00:07:49.320
do you sense anything about the old school building?

00:07:49.690 --> 00:07:52.360
Ahhh! It's Shibuya-senpai!

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:53.030
It's you.

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:56.950
If you've been having these kids tell ghost stories...

00:07:56.950 --> 00:07:58.740
Will you answer my question?

00:07:59.700 --> 00:08:02.250
Whether you really can sense spirits.

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:03.290
I can sense them.

00:08:03.670 --> 00:08:07.250
Spirits of those who died during the World War II have gathered there.

00:08:07.920 --> 00:08:10.760
I'm sure that was once a hospital.

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:13.470
I've seen a lot of injuries spirits.

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:18.510
I had no idea there was a hospital here during World War II.

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:23.440
I had heard from the school that there was a club of medics.

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:25.940
I wouldn't know.

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:28.110
Anyway, I've seen them!

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:30.280
Those who can't see spirits wouldn't understand.

00:08:30.280 --> 00:08:31.610
Shibuya-senpai,

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:33.990
maybe we should cancel things today.

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:36.200
I agree. I'm not in the mood for it.

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:37.070
Is that so?

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:38.330
Then some other time.

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:41.540
Taniyama-san,

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:45.630
do you have some spare time?

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:53.300
Um... how is he?

00:08:53.300 --> 00:08:56.090
About that... He sprained his left ankle badly

00:08:56.090 --> 00:08:57.650
and won't be able to stand for a while.

00:08:57.650 --> 00:09:00.890
I-I'm really sorry to hear that...

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:03.560
And? How do you know him?

00:09:04.100 --> 00:09:04.730
Assistant...

00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:08.560
Then that means you help him with his work?

00:09:08.560 --> 00:09:09.320
Other way around.

00:09:11.030 --> 00:09:13.320
He's the assistant; I'm the boss.

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:16.320
And that assistant can't move.

00:09:16.780 --> 00:09:18.660
You'll take responsibility for it.

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:20.160
W-Wait a minute!

00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:21.240
The camera is broken.

00:09:22.330 --> 00:09:25.620
He tried to stop you from touching the camera.

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:27.080
And that's what it resulted in...

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:29.630
Just wondering... how much is it?

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:31.050
Perhaps you would...

00:09:31.630 --> 00:09:32.880
You don't mean...

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:33.590
Um...

00:09:34.010 --> 00:09:36.510
Compensating me would be impossible for you,

00:09:36.510 --> 00:09:38.510
so you have only one choice.

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:41.180
Work as my assistant.

00:09:41.470 --> 00:09:42.850
Assistant?

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:46.270
So I'll help you with your work?

00:09:46.270 --> 00:09:47.690
Isn't that what you just heard?

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:50.520
What kind of work do you do?

00:09:50.520 --> 00:09:51.570
Ghost hunter.

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:52.820
Eh?

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:55.610
In other words, ghost exorcists.

00:09:56.900 --> 00:09:59.620
We received a request from the principal to investigate the old school.

00:09:59.620 --> 00:10:01.620
I'm with the Shibuya Psychic Research.

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:03.330
Psychic Research?

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:04.620
Is that a question?

00:10:05.960 --> 00:10:08.000
Psychic as in "shinrei",

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:09.210
and research as in "chousho".

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:12.590
In other words, Shibuya Psychic Research

00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:14.710
investigates supernatural phenomena.

00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:17.550
I'm the manager.

00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:31.830
Amazing!

00:10:31.830 --> 00:10:34.440
One week ago, this school's principal came to our office.

00:10:35.400 --> 00:10:36.490
That is good...

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:41.160
There are some strange rumours about the old school building being cursed.

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:43.160
I did some research on what happened.

00:10:43.160 --> 00:10:47.000
The old school building was used as part of the school until eighteen years ago.

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:50.170
Since that time, every year, one or two deaths have been confirmed.

00:10:50.830 --> 00:10:53.540
In that case of the demolition of the west wall,

00:10:53.540 --> 00:10:56.130
the accident where the roof collapse did, in fact, occur.

00:10:56.130 --> 00:10:57.220
However,

00:10:57.220 --> 00:10:59.590
there is no truth about workers being killed.

00:10:59.590 --> 00:11:01.430
Only 5 people were injured.

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:03.390
The reason for stopping was a worker's negligence.

00:11:04.220 --> 00:11:08.230
The original purpose of the project was to demolish a third of the building which was carried out as planned.

00:11:08.810 --> 00:11:11.520
It's true a teacher committed suicide.

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:13.230
And that was also

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:14.480
part of the reason.

00:11:15.530 --> 00:11:17.780
And the run away truck last year

00:11:17.780 --> 00:11:19.030
had something to do with it.

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:22.320
And so, work was cancelled at the time.

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:24.660
This may have been partially due to the rumours...

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:28.960
As my research shows, there's nothing that takes these stories beyond the level of rumours.

00:11:28.960 --> 00:11:30.290
As ominous as it all sounds,

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:32.710
each incident has a clear cause.

00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:34.590
This is base.

00:11:34.590 --> 00:11:35.550
Base?

00:11:36.960 --> 00:11:40.470
Base is where we'll do our observing from.

00:11:40.470 --> 00:11:42.970
T-Thanks for the explaination.

00:11:42.970 --> 00:11:44.550
Could you put the shelves together?

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:45.890
I'll start bringing in the equipment.

00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:48.350
You want me to stay here by myself?!

00:11:48.890 --> 00:11:50.730
Do you want to bring in the equiptment then?

00:11:50.730 --> 00:11:52.650
I'll have you know that some of it weighs up to 40kg.

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:54.480
I'm fine with the shelves...

00:11:55.150 --> 00:11:57.150
What's so big about 40 kilos?

00:11:57.150 --> 00:12:00.530
Like I'm some kind of weak girl who can't do it.

00:12:00.530 --> 00:12:02.030
Even so...

00:12:20.010 --> 00:12:22.180
Don't stand there like an idiot. Get to work!

00:12:23.590 --> 00:12:25.680
I hate him... that bastard.

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:28.560
What's this?

00:12:28.560 --> 00:12:31.140
Infrared and high-speed cameras

00:12:31.140 --> 00:12:33.020
are used to take pictures in dark places.

00:12:34.060 --> 00:12:36.770
And this is for thermography. It makes use of heat sensitive camera

00:12:36.770 --> 00:12:39.230
to give a visual image

00:12:39.230 --> 00:12:40.820
based on temperature.

00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:41.740
This sure is amazing.

00:12:41.740 --> 00:12:43.280
You know how to use all this?

00:12:43.460 --> 00:12:44.490
Of course.

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:46.410
Your mind and mine are very different.

00:12:46.410 --> 00:12:47.280
Ah, is that so?

00:12:47.780 --> 00:12:52.290
Of course! Naturally, there's no choice but to have you do all this.

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:54.670
But why are you hunting ghosts?

00:12:54.890 --> 00:12:56.460
Because there was a need for it.

00:12:56.460 --> 00:12:59.380
But there must have been some cases you couldn't solve?

00:12:59.380 --> 00:13:00.130
There have been none.

00:13:00.130 --> 00:13:01.510
I'm competent at what I do.

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:02.720
That sure is something!

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:04.180
Not only are you good looking, but you're very smart.

00:13:04.510 --> 00:13:06.180
Do you really think I'm good looking?

00:13:06.760 --> 00:13:07.850
Aren't you?

00:13:07.850 --> 00:13:09.560
Everyone was making a fuss over it.

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:10.850
Hm...

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:12.320
You don't have bad taste.

00:13:12.320 --> 00:13:15.310
He may be good looking, and his job status is quite impressive,

00:13:15.310 --> 00:13:18.020
but what's with that "I'm number one" attitude?!

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:22.540
From now on, you're Naru-chan!

00:13:22.540 --> 00:13:25.150
Narcissistic Naru-chan!

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:36.750
You can go home for today.

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:38.040
For today?

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:39.170
You can't be...

00:13:39.170 --> 00:13:40.290
I'll see you tomorrow.

00:13:40.960 --> 00:13:41.920
Is he serious?

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:46.380
Mai?

00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:50.260
Were you with Shibuya-senpai the entire time?

00:13:50.970 --> 00:13:52.180
What were you doing?

00:13:52.180 --> 00:13:53.680
Keiko, Michiru.

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:55.180
Eh?

00:13:55.180 --> 00:13:56.690
Psychic Research?

00:13:56.690 --> 00:13:58.900
Shibuya-san isn't an upperclassman?

00:13:58.900 --> 00:14:00.820
No, he's a ghost hunter.

00:14:00.820 --> 00:14:02.440
Ghost hunter?

00:14:02.440 --> 00:14:03.690
Taniyama-san...

00:14:05.070 --> 00:14:06.990
could you introduce me to him?

00:14:06.990 --> 00:14:09.410
Introduce you to Naru-chan?

00:14:09.410 --> 00:14:11.450
What do you mean, "Naru-chan"?

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:14.700
Because he's an amazing narcissist.

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:17.040
He's also got a rotten personality!

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:19.460
After all, I can sense spirits,

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:21.630
so maybe I can help out with something.

00:14:22.130 --> 00:14:25.050
I don't think it's such a good idea to get involved with him.

00:14:25.050 --> 00:14:26.420
He's a pro.

00:14:26.420 --> 00:14:28.340
I know more about this work that you.

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:31.850
Let's go, Mai.

00:14:32.310 --> 00:14:33.600
Y-yeah.

00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:39.850
She sure is strange.

00:14:39.850 --> 00:14:43.270
Having strange dreams and saying, "It's dangerous."

00:14:43.270 --> 00:14:45.900
Kuroda's going through the same school system as keiko and them?

00:14:45.900 --> 00:14:46.780
That's right.

00:14:46.780 --> 00:14:48.740
She says she can sense ghosts...

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:55.790
Hey now, maybe she's got the hots for Shibuya. Do you?

00:14:55.790 --> 00:14:57.750
No way! Stop that...

00:15:04.800 --> 00:15:05.710
What are you doing?

00:15:05.710 --> 00:15:07.380
Checking over last night's data.

00:15:07.380 --> 00:15:08.800
Nothing significant.

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:11.010
Hey! That's quite the load of equiptment.

00:15:11.470 --> 00:15:14.260
Seems a bit pricey for children's toys.

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:17.430
And you are?

00:15:17.430 --> 00:15:20.020
I'm the miko Matsuzaki Ayako.

00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:23.520
It seems the school principal can't rely on you, so here we are.

00:15:24.020 --> 00:15:27.320
I thought mikos were pure, innocent virgins.

00:15:27.320 --> 00:15:28.280
My, my...

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:29.490
You don't see me that way?

00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:33.490
You do seem a bit old to be a virgin.

00:15:33.490 --> 00:15:36.080
Th-That's quite the insolent tongue you have, boy.

00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:36.910
And you?

00:15:37.700 --> 00:15:40.370
You aren't Matsuzaki-san's assistant, are you?

00:15:40.960 --> 00:15:42.710
I'm a monk from Mt. Kouya.

00:15:42.710 --> 00:15:44.540
I'm Takigawa Houshou.

00:15:44.540 --> 00:15:46.670
How long have they allowed long hair in Mt. Kouya now?

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:47.630
Hakaisou...

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:50.550
A hakaisou is a monk who has left his position as a monk.

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:50.550
I've left the mountain for the time being!

00:15:50.550 --> 00:15:52.300
In any case, children's play time is over.

00:15:53.090 --> 00:15:56.760
The school principal doesn't feel that he can rely on you alone;

00:15:56.760 --> 00:15:59.350
after all, you're only a kid.

00:15:59.350 --> 00:16:00.430
Is that so?

00:16:00.430 --> 00:16:02.400
That principal is making a really big deal of this too.

00:16:02.400 --> 00:16:04.990
Bringing in so many people for such an old rundown building...

00:16:04.990 --> 00:16:06.730
That's right. I can take care of this myself.

00:16:06.950 --> 00:16:08.480
Really? I wonder about that.

00:16:10.030 --> 00:16:11.240
Thank goodness.

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:13.530
The old school building is a nest of bad spirits and it was giving me a lot of problems!

00:16:13.990 --> 00:16:14.910
Kuroda-san.

00:16:15.240 --> 00:16:17.120
I'm very sensitive to spirits,

00:16:17.120 --> 00:16:18.950
so I've been quite stressed--

00:16:18.950 --> 00:16:20.080
You're full of it.

00:16:20.790 --> 00:16:22.170
You just want to stand out, don't you?

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:24.580
Do you really believe people will pay attention to you?

00:16:25.330 --> 00:16:27.130
Y-You don't have to say that much.

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:28.590
It's the truth.

00:16:28.590 --> 00:16:30.380
That girl has no ability to sense spirits.

00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:32.430
She just want to stand out.

00:16:32.430 --> 00:16:33.680
How can you...!

00:16:36.510 --> 00:16:38.890
I'll call spirit down to haunt you.

00:16:39.850 --> 00:16:40.890
Kuroda-san.

00:16:40.890 --> 00:16:41.890
You'll regret this,

00:16:42.390 --> 00:16:43.810
fake miko.

00:16:45.440 --> 00:16:47.940
That was... a really scary look in her eyes just then.

00:16:49.650 --> 00:16:50.940
N-Ne, Naru-chan,

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:52.950
What should I do today?

00:16:54.070 --> 00:16:55.740
What did you just say just now?

00:16:56.570 --> 00:16:58.240
Did you say "Naru"?

00:16:58.240 --> 00:16:59.620
Uh, I'm sorry.

00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:00.240
Ano...

00:17:00.420 --> 00:17:01.410
Where did you hear that?

00:17:01.410 --> 00:17:02.210
Eh?

00:17:02.210 --> 00:17:04.620
Could it be that others call you that?

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:05.920
I knew it.

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:09.130
Just about anyone would think of "Narcissistic Naru-chan".

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:11.260
Hello, everyone. I've brought someone else.

00:17:11.260 --> 00:17:12.840
This is John Brown-san.

00:17:13.930 --> 00:17:15.260
I be a tickled pink.

00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:20.680
I hail from Australia. I be John Brown.

00:17:20.680 --> 00:17:22.770
I'm real pleased to meet y'all.

00:17:22.770 --> 00:17:24.100
Umm...

00:17:24.100 --> 00:17:27.980
It seems Mr. Brown learned Japanese over in Kansai area so...

00:17:24.100 --> 00:17:27.980
The Kansai-ben dialect focused around the Kyoro region.
It is often seen as comedic or frightening or as very rural.

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:31.280
Which would probably make a foreigner speaking it sound very strange.
It is used primarily for initial introductions.

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:29.150
It hurts!

00:17:29.150 --> 00:17:31.280
And you're also a senser of spirits, right?

00:17:31.280 --> 00:17:34.440
I be what you might call an exorcist.

00:17:35.990 --> 00:17:40.370
If I recall correctly for catholics, you have to be a priest before you can become an exorcist.

00:17:40.370 --> 00:17:41.540
You sure are young.

00:17:41.540 --> 00:17:42.830
You're well informed on the matter.

00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:45.330
But despite my appearance, I'm nineteen.

00:17:45.330 --> 00:17:47.220
I'm more skilled than I look.

00:17:47.220 --> 00:17:50.040
Nineteen? He's older than Naru?

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:53.300
An exorcist, a hakaisou, and a ghost hunter.

00:17:53.300 --> 00:17:57.390
If he's brought in so many people, it must mean that the principle doesn't trust me.

00:17:57.930 --> 00:18:00.470
Just watch, I'll take care of it myself.

00:18:00.850 --> 00:18:02.470
I'll also go my own way.

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:05.180
Ano.. I...

00:18:05.180 --> 00:18:06.560
Do as you wish.

00:18:06.560 --> 00:18:07.650
No, ano...

00:18:07.650 --> 00:18:09.060
Weren't we going to work together?

00:18:10.730 --> 00:18:12.360
Matsuzaki-san's voice!

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:15.570
Hurry and open it!

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:15.570
I'm going to break it down.

00:18:16.030 --> 00:18:17.240
Stand back, Ayako.

00:18:17.240 --> 00:18:18.780
I'm not ready!

00:18:19.280 --> 00:18:20.370
Alright...

00:18:22.540 --> 00:18:24.450
I was looking around when I noticed

00:18:24.450 --> 00:18:27.330
the door was closed, and I couldn't open it.

00:18:27.830 --> 00:18:29.630
There's definitely something here.

00:18:29.630 --> 00:18:30.750
No, there's nothing here.

00:18:31.210 --> 00:18:32.920
There's no sense of any presence here.

00:18:33.750 --> 00:18:35.420
I-It came out!

00:18:35.420 --> 00:18:36.630
The girl is human.

00:18:37.880 --> 00:18:39.760
Hara Masako is a spirit channeler.

00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:41.550
Spirit channeler?

00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:42.970
What a surprise.

00:18:42.970 --> 00:18:45.220
Such a famous face here.

00:18:45.220 --> 00:18:46.100
What's with you?!

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:48.270
Just because you have a cute face...

00:18:48.810 --> 00:18:52.150
you're just some TV publicity stunt.

00:18:52.150 --> 00:18:54.190
Oh? I would say that this is an honour.

00:18:54.730 --> 00:18:56.190
Why you little girl...

00:18:56.650 --> 00:18:59.740
Have I met you somewhere before?

00:19:00.070 --> 00:19:02.740
No, this is the first time we've met.

00:19:03.370 --> 00:19:04.370
Is that so?

00:19:04.370 --> 00:19:06.200
Anyway, there's no spirit here.

00:19:06.200 --> 00:19:09.670
I think it's the work of an earth spirit.

00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:11.920
I think it's a jibakurei.

00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:15.090
A jibakurei is the ghost of a person who committed suicide.

00:19:12.420 --> 00:19:15.090
Didn't something like that happen a while back?

00:19:15.090 --> 00:19:20.130
Do you mean a person that died here has been stuck here as a spirit?

00:19:20.130 --> 00:19:25.060
Right. I think he's here because he can't pass on.

00:19:26.140 --> 00:19:26.890
John,

00:19:26.890 --> 00:19:27.930
what do you think?

00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:30.560
I don't know well.

00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:34.770
But aren't houses haunted because a ghost or spirit be the reason?

00:19:34.770 --> 00:19:37.240
Spirit, a seirei?

00:19:34.770 --> 00:19:37.240
A seirei is a spirit.

00:19:37.240 --> 00:19:38.530
Ghost, a yuurei?

00:19:37.240 --> 00:19:38.530
A yuurei is a ghost, a spector.

00:19:39.360 --> 00:19:40.320
Are you listening, Mai?

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:42.700
What is it? Are you asking me?

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:44.240
You were the one asking.

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:46.290
Enough already.

00:19:46.740 --> 00:19:49.250
I'll take care of it when I get back.

00:19:49.790 --> 00:19:51.620
Constantly having to deal with this...

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:55.130
I wonder what could be bothering you.

00:19:55.630 --> 00:19:58.130
They are very strong.

00:19:58.350 --> 00:19:59.170
Kuroda-san.

00:19:59.670 --> 00:20:00.680
Move it!

00:20:04.510 --> 00:20:06.100
I was attacked!

00:20:06.100 --> 00:20:06.810
No way!

00:20:07.390 --> 00:20:08.220
Really.

00:20:08.680 --> 00:20:12.940
I was walking up here, when all of a sudden, I felt an amazing power grabbed my hair.

00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:14.110
I tried to run...

00:20:14.110 --> 00:20:15.360
It grabbed my neck.

00:20:15.900 --> 00:20:18.820
You're in the way, psychic.

00:20:19.900 --> 00:20:21.110
When was this?

00:20:21.110 --> 00:20:22.320
Just a while ago...

00:20:22.320 --> 00:20:23.700
By the lockers on the second floor.

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:24.820
That's a lie.

00:20:24.820 --> 00:20:26.240
I didn't sense any spirits.

00:20:26.240 --> 00:20:26.950
There are!

00:20:26.950 --> 00:20:28.790
There <i>are</i> spirits!

00:20:28.790 --> 00:20:29.660
Strong ones...

00:20:30.540 --> 00:20:32.210
Second floor lockers?

00:20:54.600 --> 00:20:55.400
What's wrong?

00:20:55.400 --> 00:20:56.480
Did the camera break?

00:20:56.480 --> 00:20:58.520
No, it's strange.

00:20:59.650 --> 00:21:03.320
Spirits don't normally move about.

00:21:03.950 --> 00:21:05.070
Which is it?

00:21:05.290 --> 00:21:08.580
A spirit or localized electromagnetic fluctuation.

00:21:08.760 --> 00:21:10.370
It has to be a spirit.

00:21:10.370 --> 00:21:11.580
I was attacked!

00:21:11.580 --> 00:21:12.460
Right there!

00:21:12.460 --> 00:21:14.580
But Hara-san didn't sensed any spirit.

00:21:14.920 --> 00:21:17.750
Can that person really sensed spirits?

00:21:18.460 --> 00:21:22.630
It's normal for the waves of a woman's spirit medium to fluctuate violently.

00:21:23.090 --> 00:21:26.930
Even if she can really sense spirits; at the moment, she can't.

00:21:28.010 --> 00:21:30.100
If what yo said were true...

00:21:30.100 --> 00:21:32.730
It's possible that the spirit here has aligned itself with your wavelength.

00:21:33.640 --> 00:21:34.940
Perhaps...

00:21:35.310 --> 00:21:37.060
If that's true, that means...

00:21:37.610 --> 00:21:39.980
It's our fault.

00:21:39.980 --> 00:21:42.900
Low level spirits gather when you tell ghost stories.

00:21:43.280 --> 00:21:45.030
Then they attract stronger spirits.

00:21:45.030 --> 00:21:46.660
And if that happens, there'll be trouble.

00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:50.200
So you shouldn't think of ghost stories as "fun".

00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:53.700
We... caused all if this with our ghost stories.

00:21:53.700 --> 00:21:54.540
So...

00:23:41.270 --> 00:23:54.990
Filled with Evil spirits?!

00:23:42.440 --> 00:23:47.860
Next Time, File 1 ~ Filled with Evil Spirits?! ~ #2
